    <briefdescription>
<para>Slab allocator handing out fixed-size blocks for one <ref refid="namespace_b_i_basis" kindref="compound">BIBasis</ref> type per instance. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Allocates <computeroutput><ref refid="class_b_i_basis_1_1_fast_allocator_a0c8ddde9a1607694d37947eced4954ec_1a0c8ddde9a1607694d37947eced4954ec" kindref="member">MemoryPageSize</ref></computeroutput>-byte pages from the system heap and carves each page into <computeroutput><ref refid="class_b_i_basis_1_1_fast_allocator_aff61cdc80b4912891d274b693358d176_1aff61cdc80b4912891d274b693358d176" kindref="member">TSize</ref></computeroutput>-byte cells (typically the size of one <computeroutput>VarsListNode</computeroutput> or <computeroutput><ref refid="class_b_i_basis_1_1_monom_d_l" kindref="compound">MonomDL</ref></computeroutput> etc.). Free cells are threaded into a <computeroutput><ref refid="class_b_i_basis_1_1_fast_allocator_adf9baa3723c271eb4963bf2c3ae9bc65_1adf9baa3723c271eb4963bf2c3ae9bc65" kindref="member">FreeBlock</ref></computeroutput> LIFO so <computeroutput><ref refid="class_b_i_basis_1_1_fast_allocator_a67c8e5eb0731cdfe5373971f6737ed03_1a67c8e5eb0731cdfe5373971f6737ed03" kindref="member">Allocate()</ref></computeroutput> / <computeroutput>Free(p)</computeroutput> are O(1) and avoid hitting <computeroutput>malloc</computeroutput> on the <ref refid="namespace_b_i_basis" kindref="compound">BIBasis</ref> inner loop. <computeroutput><ref refid="class_b_i_basis_1_1_fast_allocator_a6f693eca1a57a46541f47058ea501b81_1a6f693eca1a57a46541f47058ea501b81" kindref="member">ExpandMemory()</ref></computeroutput> grabs a fresh page when the free list is empty. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
